Cloudberry's pxf_fdw tests on the port, on one node and on a cluster: the
differences from Cloudberry's expected output that have been reviewed, and
are the port's for a reason of its own.

Each file is one test's difference in the form ../../singlenode/canon.pl
gives it, named for the expected output it differs from; a file named
<test>.<target>.diff is the difference of one target alone, one_node or
cluster.  run.sh counts a test as passing when gpdiff.pl, under Cloudberry's
init file and the port's, finds no difference or exactly the file's.

  pxf_fdw_foreign_table  PostgreSQL 19's COPY says an option CSV alone takes
                         in its own words, "COPY QUOTE requires CSV mode",
                         where PostgreSQL 16's, which Cloudberry's test masks
                         to "quote available only in CSV mode", said "COPY
                         quote available only in CSV mode".  The validator
                         asks PostgreSQL's COPY about the options it has, as
                         Cloudberry's does.
